<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manuel I of Portugal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1469">1469</a>–<a href="/years/1521">1521</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Manuel the Fortunate · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-aviz">House of Aviz</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manuel I was King of Portugal from 1495 to 1521, known as the Fortunate. His reign saw <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasco-da-gama">Vasco da Gama</a>'s voyage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, Cabral's landing in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> and the building of a Portuguese empire in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>, as well as fortified posts on the Atlantic coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>. Spice-trade wealth paid for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manueline-style">Manueline style</a> of architecture named after him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manuel-i-of-portugal.jpg" alt="Manuel I of Portugal" width="320" height="473" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gilles Messian from Paris, France · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_of_King_Manuel_I_of_Portugal_by_Nicolau_Chanterene.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1512 King <b>Manuel I of Portugal</b> had the garrison withdrawn, and Kilwa remained only a nominal vassal.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kilwa-sultanate">Kilwa Sultanate · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Under <b>Manuel I</b> the Portuguese built or seized Atlantic posts at Agadir, Safi, Azemmour and Mazagan between 1505 and 1514.</blockquote><a href="/state/portuguese-morocco">Portuguese Morocco</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/portugal">Portugal</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/portugal">Portugal</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=38.71,-9.14&amp;year=1502" aria-label="Lisbon on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4323 775 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Manuel I of Portugal"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4773 1045h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4773 1045h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=38.71,-9.14&amp;year=1502">What was here in 1502? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
